<title>USA: Northwest Airlines files $250 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>Northwest Airlines files $250 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northwest Airlines Inc filed Friday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission a shelf offering of up to $250 million of debt securities and warrants to purchase debt securities guaranteed by parent company Northwest Airlines Corp.</p>
<p>Together with previous offerings, the Minnesota-based airline's offering totals $500 million.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes, according to the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
